      "side": 1,
      "message": "Trusty supports and needs this call, but other TEEs might not. In that case they\u0027d return `FFA_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED`, maybe we should ignore that error here.\n\nThe remaining errors that this call can return, per the spec:\n* `FFA_RET_INVALID_PARAMETERS`: _Unrecognized endpoint or vCPU ID_. The TEE could theoretically return this if it doesn\u0027t support `FFA_RUN` but it\u0027s unlikely. This would probably happen if we passed in a wrong `dest`, so we should report it as an actual error.\n* `FFA_RET_DENIED`: _Callee is not in a state to handle this request_ or _Caller is not allowed to invoke this ABI_. It means we\u0027re doing something wrong, so we should return an error.\n* `FFA_RET_BUSY`: _vCPU is busy and caller must retry later_. It makes sense to return `-EBUSY` here, but it sounds like the hypervisor should retry?\n* `FFA_RET_ABORTED`: the TEE aborted so the hypervisor probably should as well.\n\nWe can fix this in a separate CL if that\u0027s easier.",
      "revId": "d25a0675d384f639467adddbebba10240c50d5c8",
